What makes a servo different?
Servos
Servos don’t move automatically when you apply power to them.  They have a signal pin, and wait for the signal to tell them what position to move to.

Some servos can rotate 360°, though most have a limit of 180°.
How can we use a signal to specify the servo position?
Servo vs. Motor:
Servos move 0 to 180 degrees
Servos can move clockwise and counterclockwise
Servos are controlled with a signal wire
On servo:
Brown  	= Ground
Red       	= 5V
Orange 	= Signal
Any ideas how we would write the code for this circuit?
Servo understands timed pulse
Different pulse widths -> Different positions
